# alloc_heavy — maximal Value / Env / string / call churn.
# Reconstruction of #1675's workload of the same name (its scratch file was
# never committed; see poollayers-REPORT.md "alloc_heavy reconstruction").
# Each call allocates a fresh env (Env freelist + call-env recycling), short-lived
# NUMs (Value freelist), and a short string.
# CodSpeed sizing (SYNC11 cont4): outer calls 20,000 -> 5,000; inner work(50)
# unchanged. The original took 101 s in hosted CPU simulation; one quarter
# of the calls keeps the same allocation churn below ~60 s per target.
define work(n) as:
    s is 0
    j is 0
    loop while j < n:
        local a is (j * 3) + 1
        local b is (a - j) * 2
        local t is "v" + (str of (j % 100))
        s is s + a + b + (len of t)
        j is j + 1
    return s
total is 0
for i in range of 5000:
    total is total + (work of 50)
print of total
